        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e46bcecd-e1be-5a56-8416-60e6241829f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bobby Moore, Geoff Hurst, Martin Peters, Pelé\n- Organizations: West Ham United, 1860 Munich, England national football team\n- Events: 1964–65 European Cup Winners' Cup, 1966 FIFA World Cup Final\n- Places: Wembley Stadium\n- Concepts: football defending, player reputation\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1964–65 European Cup Winners' Cup, West Ham United won the tournament by defeating 1860 Munich in the final at Wembley Stadium.\n- In the 1964–65 European Cup Winners' Cup final season, Bobby Moore captained West Ham United, and the team also included Geoff Hurst and Martin Peters.\n- In 1966, Bobby Moore, Geoff Hurst, and Martin Peters starred for England's World Cup-winning side.\n- Bobby Moore is widely regarded as one of the greatest defenders of all time.\n- Pelé said that Bobby Moore was the greatest defender Pelé had ever played against.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
